  "label": "audience",
  "description": "The intended audience for this meme is individuals familiar with internet meme culture, particularly those who engage in self-deprecating humor and enjoy relatable, casual online content. The use of 'y'all' suggests an appeal to audiences comfortable with Southern U.S. English or informal, conversational internet slang. The exaggerated movie theater reaction trope is widely recognized in meme culture as a humorous device for contrasting intense reactions with mundane situations. The target community is broadly internet-savvy users who appreciate the comedic irony of admitting they are about to share something trivial ('stupid post') and expect others to react with exaggerated shock, creating a shared, self-referential humor experience.",
